1
00:00:02,332 --> 00:00:05,753
THE HUSBAND

2
00:00:10,007 --> 00:00:11,133
THIS SERIES IS FICTITIOUS

3
00:00:11,216 --> 00:00:13,844
CHILDREN WERE FILMED SAFELY
GEN AI WAS USED IN SELECT SCENES

4
00:00:40,788 --> 00:00:41,789
Are you okay?

5
00:00:43,290 --> 00:00:44,375
Yeah, I'm fine.

6
00:00:44,458 --> 00:00:46,043
[sighs]

7
00:00:48,670 --> 00:00:49,671
[grunts]

8
00:00:55,260 --> 00:00:56,261
We'd better hurry.

9
00:00:57,721 --> 00:00:59,181
We're almost there. Come on!

10
00:01:03,352 --> 00:01:04,603
[grunts]

11
00:01:14,738 --> 00:01:16,782
[grunting, panting]

12
00:01:33,340 --> 00:01:34,341
I made it.

13
00:01:35,008 --> 00:01:36,009
Come on!

14
00:02:02,828 --> 00:02:03,871
[grunts]

15
00:02:17,217 --> 00:02:18,469
[gasping]

16
00:02:25,517 --> 00:02:26,518
You all right?

17
00:02:27,311 --> 00:02:28,312
Yeah, I'm good!

18
00:02:49,791 --> 00:02:50,792
What do you think?

19
00:02:51,793 --> 00:02:54,046
Mmm. It's nice.

20
00:02:57,174 --> 00:02:58,884
I'm glad we came.

21
00:03:02,679 --> 00:03:04,014
[sighs]

22
00:03:06,433 --> 00:03:07,559
[chuckles]

23
00:03:21,156 --> 00:03:23,659
[director] So far, a damaged spinal cord

24
00:03:23,742 --> 00:03:27,621
has been deemed
almost impossible to treat.

25
00:03:28,622 --> 00:03:33,252
And Woori Together Medical Center
was the first institution in the world

26
00:03:33,335 --> 00:03:36,463
to attempt merging
3D bio-printing technology

27
00:03:36,546 --> 00:03:42,302
and stem cell therapy
to restore a damaged spinal cord.

28
00:03:43,762 --> 00:03:47,683
After three years of clinical trials

29
00:03:47,766 --> 00:03:52,646
with 32 patients
who had complete spinal cord injuries,

30
00:03:52,729 --> 00:03:57,568
approximately 80% showed
signs of sensory recovery,

31
00:03:57,651 --> 00:04:00,529
and over 60% showed

32
00:04:00,612 --> 00:04:05,492
limited but voluntary movement.

33
00:04:05,993 --> 00:04:07,661
-[relative] Yes, keep going.
-Just one more time.

34
00:04:07,744 --> 00:04:09,413
You got to keep moving.

35
00:04:11,164 --> 00:04:13,000
That's it. Yes, well done.

36
00:04:13,083 --> 00:04:16,253
Here, a patient who was
completely paralyzed for the past…

37
00:04:16,336 --> 00:04:19,214
-[phone buzzes]
-…ten years is moving his toes.
STYLE
::cue()

38
00:04:20,007 --> 00:04:23,510
We have a long way to go
until they can walk again.

39
00:04:24,344 --> 00:04:28,473
However, we have seen
undeniable potential.

40
00:04:29,516 --> 00:04:32,644
And I'd like to thank Dr. Kang Taeju,

41
00:04:32,728 --> 00:04:36,732
Director of Woori Together Medical Center,
for showing us the way.

42
00:04:38,525 --> 00:04:41,069
Dr. Kang, please share a few words.

43
00:04:45,157 --> 00:04:46,408
I'm sorry, Dr. Ko.

44
00:04:46,491 --> 00:04:49,536
I've been paged to the OR
for an emergency.

45
00:04:49,620 --> 00:04:50,912
Please excuse me.

46
00:04:51,538 --> 00:04:52,956
I'm sorry.

47
00:04:53,040 --> 00:04:55,334
[crowd murmuring]

48
00:05:03,675 --> 00:05:07,054
Every second counts
for an emergency patient.

49
00:05:07,137 --> 00:05:08,722
We hope you understand.

50
00:05:10,098 --> 00:05:13,143
But while Dr. Kang is away,

51
00:05:13,226 --> 00:05:18,398
Dr. Ko will give you a more
in-depth explanation of this project.

52
00:05:19,066 --> 00:05:20,901
Please give him a big hand.

53
00:05:20,984 --> 00:05:22,653
DOUBLE-CHECK CONSENT!
SURGICAL CONSENT,

54
00:05:22,736 --> 00:05:25,530
BLOOD TRANSFUSION CONSENT,
AND PCA CONSENT

55
00:05:30,202 --> 00:05:31,203
[Taeju] Freer.

56
00:05:43,048 --> 00:05:45,050
WOORI TOGETHER MEDICAL CENTER

57
00:05:48,220 --> 00:05:50,472
-[Dr. Ko] …we can.
-[laughter]

58
00:05:50,555 --> 00:05:51,556
Hello.

59
00:05:56,603 --> 00:05:58,438
How are you, sir?

60
00:05:59,189 --> 00:06:00,357
[patient] Good to see you.

61
00:06:01,274 --> 00:06:02,651
I've just wrapped up the event.

62
00:06:02,734 --> 00:06:04,611
Okay. Good work.

63
00:06:05,404 --> 00:06:08,573
So, how are you feeling today?
Are you doing all right?

64
00:06:08,657 --> 00:06:11,868
Hmm. I'm not all right at all.

65
00:06:12,744 --> 00:06:14,871
Oh… Is something bothering you?

66
00:06:14,955 --> 00:06:18,208
I'm starting to see things.

67
00:06:18,291 --> 00:06:21,044
[chuckles] He means he's hungry.

68
00:06:21,128 --> 00:06:22,295
What?

69
00:06:22,379 --> 00:06:25,257
This fasting thing is killing me.

70
00:06:26,716 --> 00:06:28,510
[Dr. Ko] Just think of it as a long nap.

71
00:06:28,593 --> 00:06:30,720
The surgery will be over in no time.

72
00:06:30,804 --> 00:06:31,930
Isn't that right, Ms. Ko?

73
00:06:32,013 --> 00:06:33,181
Of course.

74
00:06:33,265 --> 00:06:37,561
Dr. Kang is number one
in the field of spinal cord microsurgery.

75
00:06:37,644 --> 00:06:39,729
[Taeju] We'll begin
Chairman Kim Manseong's

76
00:06:39,813 --> 00:06:41,440
spinal stenosis surgery in 30 minutes.

77
00:06:41,523 --> 00:06:42,691
[staff] Yes, Doctor.

78
00:06:47,612 --> 00:06:50,198
-[spouse] Please, I'm begging you!
-[guard] Calm down, ma'am!

79
00:06:50,282 --> 00:06:51,867
[spouse] Please help my husband!

80
00:06:51,950 --> 00:06:53,702
-All right. Could you please wait…
-Just…

81
00:06:53,785 --> 00:06:56,830
At least let a doctor see him!

82
00:06:56,913 --> 00:06:58,415
[guard] We still need you to calm down.

83
00:06:58,498 --> 00:06:59,749
What's going on over there?

84
00:07:00,584 --> 00:07:02,544
She's screaming
that her husband needs surgery.

85
00:07:03,128 --> 00:07:04,963
-Is it an emergency?
-Yeah.

86
00:07:05,547 --> 00:07:08,925
But all the surgeons on call
are in surgery right now,

87
00:07:09,009 --> 00:07:12,387
so we told her she has to wait,
but it's no use.

88
00:07:12,846 --> 00:07:16,016
She says she'll kill herself right here
and now if he can't get surgery.

89
00:07:16,475 --> 00:07:17,476
Geez.

90
00:07:21,396 --> 00:07:24,316
Please help my husband!

91
00:07:24,399 --> 00:07:25,609
Yes, we understand,

92
00:07:25,692 --> 00:07:27,652
-but no one can operate on him right now.
-[wailing]

93
00:07:27,736 --> 00:07:29,905
So please stop blocking the way
and wait outside.

94
00:07:29,988 --> 00:07:32,824
Every hospital we've been to
said the same thing!

95
00:07:32,908 --> 00:07:33,992
[husband wailing]

96
00:07:34,075 --> 00:07:35,911
If he doesn't get help, he's going to die!

97
00:07:35,994 --> 00:07:39,080
This isn't going to change anything.
Hey, get them out of here.

98
00:07:39,164 --> 00:07:41,333
-No, please…
-Come on.

99
00:07:41,416 --> 00:07:43,919
-Let's go.
-Please! No!

100
00:07:44,294 --> 00:07:45,837
Sir!

101
00:07:46,588 --> 00:07:49,549
-[husband continues wailing]
-[wife] Please! Stop! Don't do this!

102
00:07:49,633 --> 00:07:50,634
Hold on.

103
00:07:53,220 --> 00:07:54,221
Dr. Kang.

104
00:07:57,057 --> 00:07:58,767
What seems to be the problem?

105
00:07:59,309 --> 00:08:04,272
His back, hips, and legs all hurt so bad
that he can't even walk properly.

106
00:08:04,856 --> 00:08:08,026
He can't go to the bathroom,
and he can't tell if he needs to go.

107
00:08:09,110 --> 00:08:11,530
Sir, we're going to try
pointing your toes up, okay?

108
00:08:11,613 --> 00:08:14,741
-[wailing]
-[Taeju] You can't move it, can you?

109
00:08:16,993 --> 00:08:18,954
[husband] I can't do it.

110
00:08:19,037 --> 00:08:20,247
When did this start?

111
00:08:21,039 --> 00:08:24,084
He was moving the table yesterday,
and he suddenly said his back hurt.

112
00:08:24,167 --> 00:08:25,460
He's been like this since.

113
00:08:25,544 --> 00:08:26,795
Around what time?

114
00:08:26,878 --> 00:08:29,297
It was right after breakfast, so 9 a.m.

115
00:08:29,381 --> 00:08:31,800
[husband continues wailing]

116
00:08:36,096 --> 00:08:37,931
-Wait a minute.
-Ms. Ko.

117
00:08:38,640 --> 00:08:40,392
-What's going on?
-Well…

118
00:08:42,519 --> 00:08:43,770
Did you get the MRI yet?

119
00:08:43,854 --> 00:08:46,106
-[nurse] We should have it any minute now.
-Do we have an OR?

120
00:08:46,189 --> 00:08:49,734
OR Three. Anesthesia is almost here, too.

121
00:08:49,818 --> 00:08:51,278
Dr. Kang.

122
00:08:52,863 --> 00:08:54,155
We need to talk.

123
00:08:54,239 --> 00:08:55,323
Not now, sorry.

124
00:08:55,407 --> 00:08:58,618
You can't change the surgery schedule
for a VIP patient as you wish.

125
00:08:59,369 --> 00:09:02,414
This will put us in a tight spot.
Did you even think about that?
STYLE
::cue()

126
00:09:05,292 --> 00:09:06,293
I'm sorry.

127
00:09:06,877 --> 00:09:07,878
You're sorry?

128
00:09:12,424 --> 00:09:13,758
I'm sick of hearing that.

129
00:09:15,051 --> 00:09:16,761
You got anything else?

130
00:09:28,106 --> 00:09:29,900
He's got cauda equina.

131
00:09:30,650 --> 00:09:33,904
If he doesn't get surgery now,
he'll have to live with a disability.

132
00:09:33,987 --> 00:09:36,823
CAUDA EQUINA SYNDROME: LEG PARALYSIS
AND BLADDER/BOWL DYSFUNCTION

133
00:09:36,907 --> 00:09:39,576
CAUSED BY COMPRESSION OF NERVES
AT THE END OF THE SPINAL CORD

134
00:09:55,342 --> 00:09:57,135
This hospital has a schedule to stick to.

135
00:09:59,095 --> 00:10:01,014
You'll do Chairman Kim's surgery first.

136
00:10:01,598 --> 00:10:04,142
Chairman Kim's is a simple procedure.

137
00:10:04,225 --> 00:10:07,062
This man's out of time.
He may never walk again.

138
00:10:07,520 --> 00:10:09,147
Here we go again.

139
00:10:10,565 --> 00:10:13,068
There's always something more important.

140
00:10:14,069 --> 00:10:15,987
Something more urgent.

141
00:10:30,251 --> 00:10:31,962
-[Taeju] Let's go.
-Yes, Doctor.

142
00:10:59,698 --> 00:11:01,574
Okay, let's verify the patient's identity.

143
00:11:01,658 --> 00:11:03,868
Park Yeongjun, 42-year-old male.

144
00:11:03,952 --> 00:11:06,162
It's an emergency decompression
for cauda equina.

145
00:11:06,246 --> 00:11:07,998
Going in for a laminectomy.

146
00:11:08,081 --> 00:11:09,499
Anesthesia, any issues?

147
00:11:09,582 --> 00:11:12,002
-All clear.
-Okay, we're going up. Blade.

148
00:11:19,592 --> 00:11:21,636
Dr. Kang. Stop this at once.

149
00:11:25,473 --> 00:11:28,685
Dr. Ko, you can't be in here.

150
00:11:28,768 --> 00:11:32,564
You know better than anyone that the OR
is a restricted zone during a procedure.

151
00:11:33,064 --> 00:11:34,774
You haven't even made an incision yet!

152
00:11:35,358 --> 00:11:38,194
Put this on hold,
and stick to the original schedule.

153
00:11:39,029 --> 00:11:41,740
This patient is critical.
It’s an emergency cauda equina case.

154
00:11:41,823 --> 00:11:44,784
Don't you hear me?
I don't give a damn what it is!

155
00:11:44,868 --> 00:11:47,454
You're putting
the entire hospital at risk!

156
00:11:48,371 --> 00:11:51,708
Do you have any idea how much Chairman Kim
has poured into this facility?

157
00:11:52,667 --> 00:11:55,920
Stop this procedure
and get Chairman Kim on the table first.

158
00:11:57,380 --> 00:11:58,381
Now!

159
00:12:01,468 --> 00:12:03,636
-Please get out.
-What?

160
00:12:04,387 --> 00:12:05,805
I said, please get out of here.

161
00:12:07,515 --> 00:12:08,516
What did you say?

162
00:12:09,601 --> 00:12:11,603
I said, get the hell out of here!

163
00:12:12,187 --> 00:12:13,938
[phone buzzing]

164
00:12:14,939 --> 00:12:15,940
Yes?

165
00:12:18,359 --> 00:12:19,736
Wait, what?

166
00:12:23,782 --> 00:12:25,992
[Taeju] Did you not hear me?
Get out of here right now!

167
00:12:30,413 --> 00:12:32,749
Please leave. Right now.

168
00:12:32,832 --> 00:12:35,085
Dr. Kang, I think you're out of line.

169
00:12:35,794 --> 00:12:37,253
This is my OR.

170
00:12:39,297 --> 00:12:40,423
Please leave.

171
00:12:43,551 --> 00:12:46,054
This is what I get
for letting you into my family.

172
00:13:18,878 --> 00:13:21,089
All right, let's resume.

173
00:13:21,589 --> 00:13:22,590
Blade.

174
00:13:39,065 --> 00:13:43,987
THE HUSBAND
STYLE
::cue()

175
00:13:48,074 --> 00:13:49,409
[alarm chimes]

176
00:13:49,492 --> 00:13:50,994
SATURDAY, FEBRUARY 7
ALARM

177
00:13:53,913 --> 00:13:56,416
[alarm continues chiming]

178
00:13:59,168 --> 00:14:00,712
[alarm stops]

179
00:14:01,212 --> 00:14:02,547
[door opens]

180
00:14:33,077 --> 00:14:35,038
Do you want some coffee? I just made it.

181
00:14:37,498 --> 00:14:40,293
[coffee machine beeps, whirs]

182
00:14:46,174 --> 00:14:49,302
I had no choice yesterday.
That man was running out of time.

183
00:14:51,763 --> 00:14:53,765
Plus, Chairman Kim's surgery went well.

184
00:15:03,149 --> 00:15:05,944
All's well that ends well, huh?
Is that what you're saying?

185
00:15:07,195 --> 00:15:10,615
All right, I'm sorry
I didn't stick to the schedule.

186
00:15:10,698 --> 00:15:13,493
But it was only delayed by an hour, so…

187
00:15:14,535 --> 00:15:15,536
Only an hour?

188
00:15:16,746 --> 00:15:18,414
He's not just another VIP.

189
00:15:18,498 --> 00:15:21,042
He's the chairman
of our biggest corporate sponsor.

190
00:15:21,125 --> 00:15:23,962
Seyun, it was an emergency patient.

191
00:15:24,045 --> 00:15:25,463
I had no choice.

192
00:15:26,255 --> 00:15:29,384
Had we not operated on him,
he would never have walked again.

193
00:15:29,467 --> 00:15:32,679
Our hospital has
a very specific set of rules.

194
00:15:33,638 --> 00:15:35,223
And you completely ignored it.

195
00:15:35,306 --> 00:15:37,225
Are those the hospital's rules,

196
00:15:38,309 --> 00:15:39,978
or you and your dad's rules?

197
00:15:40,061 --> 00:15:41,396
What?

198
00:15:42,146 --> 00:15:43,147
Nothing.

199
00:15:43,231 --> 00:15:45,900
I'll apologize to your dad
and Chairman Kim personally.

200
00:15:46,484 --> 00:15:47,735
Yeah, you do that.

201
00:15:52,198 --> 00:15:53,866
[tires squealing]

202
00:16:07,088 --> 00:16:10,967
Father, I was out of line yesterday.
I'm really sorry.

203
00:16:12,427 --> 00:16:14,429
That was really something, you know that?

204
00:16:15,096 --> 00:16:17,181
"Get out of my OR"?

205
00:16:18,182 --> 00:16:20,351
I get that we're both
technically directors here.

206
00:16:20,435 --> 00:16:22,645
WOORI TOGETHER MEDICAL CENTER
DIRECTOR KO DONGCHAN

207
00:16:22,729 --> 00:16:24,230
But you assume we're equals?

208
00:16:25,106 --> 00:16:26,649
Is that what you think?

209
00:16:27,400 --> 00:16:29,902
I built this hospital from the ground up,

210
00:16:29,986 --> 00:16:32,822
just to be kicked out
by my own son-in-law!

211
00:16:34,449 --> 00:16:38,870
You see, with an emergency at hand,
I wasn't thinking clearly.

212
00:16:38,953 --> 00:16:40,496
I'm really sorry.

213
00:16:41,205 --> 00:16:43,708
[scoffs, sighs]

214
00:16:44,917 --> 00:16:46,586
And the press briefing?

215
00:16:47,128 --> 00:16:50,423
Do you have any idea
what they were all saying after you left?

216
00:16:51,466 --> 00:16:55,178
Do you have any idea
how Seyun had to clean up that mess?

217
00:16:55,261 --> 00:17:00,016
And Chairman Kim was so furious
that he refused our treatment.

218
00:17:01,059 --> 00:17:03,394
So she barely managed
to convince him into…

219
00:17:04,354 --> 00:17:05,355
[sighs]

220
00:17:08,066 --> 00:17:11,361
I promise it'll never happen again.

221
00:17:11,444 --> 00:17:12,445
I'm sorry.

222
00:17:12,528 --> 00:17:13,863
Is that right?

223
00:17:13,946 --> 00:17:16,074
It must be nice being you.
STYLE
::cue()

224
00:17:16,783 --> 00:17:18,743
You go around
making a mess left and right,

225
00:17:18,826 --> 00:17:21,162
and Seyun does all the cleanup.

226
00:17:21,829 --> 00:17:23,164
[sighs]

227
00:17:25,708 --> 00:17:27,502
I'm really sorry, Father.

228
00:17:28,086 --> 00:17:30,797
Get out.
I can't even stand seeing you right now!

229
00:17:46,646 --> 00:17:49,440
Dr. Kang must've gotten
an earful from Dr. Ko.

230
00:17:49,524 --> 00:17:51,859
He looks totally deflated.

231
00:17:51,943 --> 00:17:53,820
[nurse] What's with him these days?

232
00:17:53,903 --> 00:17:56,781
He never used to butt heads
with Dr. Ko like that.

233
00:17:56,864 --> 00:17:58,032
Beats me.

234
00:17:58,116 --> 00:17:59,784
It was just a matter of time.

235
00:17:59,867 --> 00:18:02,745
Knowing him,
I'd say this was bound to happen.

236
00:18:03,287 --> 00:18:06,290
Then you should've done
something beforehand, Dr. Choi.

237
00:18:06,374 --> 00:18:09,043
-Yeah, exactly.
-What was I supposed to do?

238
00:18:09,627 --> 00:18:11,838
You think he'd listen to me?

239
00:18:13,756 --> 00:18:17,093
We have to walk on eggshells
when he gets like that.

240
00:18:17,176 --> 00:18:18,511
[elevator dings]

241
00:18:25,393 --> 00:18:26,727
[sighs softly]

242
00:18:27,311 --> 00:18:28,312
[Dr. Choi] Dr. Cha.

243
00:18:31,691 --> 00:18:33,025
Would you like some coffee?

244
00:18:35,319 --> 00:18:36,320
Maybe later.

245
00:18:50,751 --> 00:18:52,462
-[Taeju] Are you going somewhere?
-Yeah.

246
00:18:53,212 --> 00:18:54,297
For an off-site meeting.

247
00:18:56,382 --> 00:18:57,383
Thank you.

248
00:18:58,384 --> 00:18:59,385
For what?

249
00:19:00,636 --> 00:19:02,305
Your dad told me.

250
00:19:03,598 --> 00:19:06,350
About the press briefing
and the situation with Chairman Kim.

251
00:19:07,351 --> 00:19:08,895
You covered for me.

252
00:19:10,104 --> 00:19:12,315
I was just doing my job
as the board director.

253
00:19:13,733 --> 00:19:19,155
Yeah, I know. It's just good to know
you might still be on my side.

254
00:19:22,033 --> 00:19:23,743
Don't think I did all that for you.

255
00:19:25,077 --> 00:19:27,371
I can't let this hospital
end up like us, can I?

256
00:19:27,455 --> 00:19:29,123
[elevator dings]

257
00:19:55,816 --> 00:19:57,610
[phone ringing]

258
00:20:07,745 --> 00:20:10,498
[phone continues ringing]

259
00:20:13,918 --> 00:20:15,211
[gasps]

260
00:20:15,294 --> 00:20:17,171
Vitals are dropping.
Give me an amp of epi.

261
00:20:17,255 --> 00:20:19,465
The patient is flatlining.
Keep compressing.

262
00:20:19,549 --> 00:20:21,425
[Seyun] Please, no…

263
00:20:21,509 --> 00:20:22,843
[doctor] Get the crash cart in here!

264
00:20:22,927 --> 00:20:25,096
-[monitor flatlining]
-[panting]

265
00:20:26,597 --> 00:20:28,057
[sobbing]

266
00:20:34,063 --> 00:20:36,148
[horn honking]
STYLE
::cue()

267
00:20:50,288 --> 00:20:51,330
Hey, Dr. Kang…

268
00:20:53,291 --> 00:20:54,834
[sighs]

269
00:21:08,139 --> 00:21:10,224
STAIRWELL
FIRE DOOR, KEEP CLOSED

270
00:21:10,308 --> 00:21:12,852
DO NOT PLACE OBJECTS
NEAR FIRE DOOR

271
00:21:22,153 --> 00:21:23,154
I knew you'd be here.

272
00:21:24,405 --> 00:21:25,448
Hey, what's up?

273
00:21:26,282 --> 00:21:27,575
Do you want coffee?

274
00:21:27,658 --> 00:21:28,868
No, I'm fine.

275
00:21:29,577 --> 00:21:31,912
And you should lay off
the instant coffee, Doc.

276
00:21:31,996 --> 00:21:33,414
It's pure sugar, this thing.

277
00:21:35,082 --> 00:21:37,251
Got yourself a cozy little cave here, huh?

278
00:21:44,008 --> 00:21:45,968
What the… The lock still doesn't work.

279
00:21:47,094 --> 00:21:49,972
I told them this is a major security risk.

280
00:21:50,556 --> 00:21:51,641
Geez.

281
00:21:55,561 --> 00:21:56,896
You know, I was surprised.

282
00:21:57,980 --> 00:21:59,565
In the OR, I mean.

283
00:22:00,066 --> 00:22:04,403
I've known you since med school,
but I'd never seen that side of you.

284
00:22:06,989 --> 00:22:09,659
Are you doing all right?
I know it's been rough.

285
00:22:10,993 --> 00:22:14,121
Father-in-law-slash-boss, wife-slash-boss…

286
00:22:14,205 --> 00:22:15,289
Which is harder?

287
00:22:15,998 --> 00:22:17,124
Both pretty hard.

288
00:22:17,208 --> 00:22:18,709
[chuckles]

289
00:22:20,336 --> 00:22:22,630
I take it things
are still not so great at home?

290
00:22:22,713 --> 00:22:24,298
[sighs]

291
00:22:26,175 --> 00:22:29,178
How long will you keep this up for?
The tension will make you both wither.

292
00:22:30,471 --> 00:22:31,764
Tell me about it.

293
00:22:33,641 --> 00:22:35,393
Try having a real conversation.

294
00:22:36,936 --> 00:22:39,522
Okay, so how do you have this
"real conversation"?

295
00:22:40,064 --> 00:22:41,691
What do you mean how?

296
00:22:41,774 --> 00:22:44,026
You just be honest with each other.

297
00:22:45,945 --> 00:22:47,905
And what if that makes things worse?

298
00:22:48,280 --> 00:22:49,657
What do you have to lose?

299
00:22:49,740 --> 00:22:51,075
You're already at rock bottom.

300
00:22:53,119 --> 00:22:56,163
Trust me,
there are levels beneath rock bottom.

301
00:22:58,040 --> 00:22:59,792
You still have to do something.

302
00:22:59,875 --> 00:23:01,877
Because if you don't, your marriage…

303
00:23:03,003 --> 00:23:04,255
It'll really be over.

304
00:23:15,141 --> 00:23:16,600
[car beeps]

305
00:23:21,522 --> 00:23:22,523
[Taeju] Hey, you're home.

306
00:23:28,279 --> 00:23:30,322
I thought I'd make us dinner.

307
00:23:30,406 --> 00:23:31,574
Let's eat together.

308
00:23:34,702 --> 00:23:36,871
Remember that pajeon place
at the foot of Bukhansan?

309
00:23:36,954 --> 00:23:38,247
You used to love that place.

310
00:23:39,123 --> 00:23:41,792
You sure had a big appetite
for such a tiny girl.

311
00:23:42,501 --> 00:23:43,919
I did my best,

312
00:23:45,171 --> 00:23:46,630
but I don't know if it's as good.

313
00:23:49,425 --> 00:23:50,676
I got some makgeolli too.

314
00:23:51,886 --> 00:23:53,262
I know it's your favorite.

315
00:23:54,638 --> 00:23:55,848
Have a seat.

316
00:23:58,017 --> 00:24:01,520
Man, I don't know why makgeolli
tasted so good back then.

317
00:24:02,730 --> 00:24:04,148
I've already eaten.

318
00:24:05,316 --> 00:24:07,818
Oh. Really?

319
00:24:07,902 --> 00:24:10,780
Well, why don't
we just have a drink, then?

320
00:24:11,822 --> 00:24:13,032
I don't feel like drinking.

321
00:24:15,409 --> 00:24:16,911
Wait, Seyun.

322
00:24:18,579 --> 00:24:20,456
I made it just for you.

323
00:24:20,998 --> 00:24:22,416
Just sit with me for a while.

324
00:24:23,125 --> 00:24:24,460
I said I don't want to.

325
00:24:25,461 --> 00:24:28,714
I'm just asking you to sit with me.
Is that so hard?

326
00:24:34,678 --> 00:24:36,388
[door closes]
STYLE
::cue()

327
00:24:58,160 --> 00:24:59,411
[sighs]

328
00:25:06,919 --> 00:25:07,920
[door opens]

329
00:25:10,422 --> 00:25:11,841
Did you change your mind?

330
00:25:17,471 --> 00:25:18,764
I'll pour you one.

331
00:25:18,848 --> 00:25:19,932
It's fine. I got it.

332
00:25:20,015 --> 00:25:21,934
I just want to do
something for you for once.

333
00:25:22,017 --> 00:25:24,019
-I said, it's fine.
-Come on, just let me…

334
00:25:29,733 --> 00:25:31,527
I said I'd do it myself!

335
00:25:33,279 --> 00:25:34,655
I told you I'd do it.

336
00:25:34,738 --> 00:25:36,115
What is wrong with…

337
00:25:46,333 --> 00:25:47,459
I'm sorry.

338
00:25:51,839 --> 00:25:54,717
But does this make you that mad?

339
00:25:55,217 --> 00:25:56,969
This is why our marriage isn't working.

340
00:25:58,345 --> 00:26:01,056
Even the smallest things turn into a mess
when we're together.

341
00:26:02,600 --> 00:26:04,059
I'll fix this up.

342
00:26:04,685 --> 00:26:05,895
It's just like our marriage.

343
00:26:06,937 --> 00:26:08,564
Shattered to pieces.

344
00:26:12,276 --> 00:26:15,446
You'll fix it? What's broken is broken.

345
00:26:16,697 --> 00:26:19,199
You can glue it together,
but it'll never be whole again.

346
00:26:19,742 --> 00:26:21,410
Are you really going to be like this?

347
00:26:21,744 --> 00:26:23,203
You always do this.

348
00:26:23,704 --> 00:26:25,873
It's always, "It's okay, we'll try again."

349
00:26:25,956 --> 00:26:27,416
As if nothing ever happened.

350
00:26:29,001 --> 00:26:31,295
What do you want from me?

351
00:26:32,922 --> 00:26:34,173
What do you want me to do?

352
00:26:34,256 --> 00:26:35,674
Tell me, I'm all ears.

353
00:26:36,884 --> 00:26:39,345
Because I honestly don't know
what more I can do.

354
00:26:39,845 --> 00:26:41,889
So just keep on living
like you always have.

355
00:26:42,890 --> 00:26:44,892
That's the only thing you know how to do.

356
00:26:54,360 --> 00:26:56,362
I'm going to fix it up, okay?

357
00:27:05,329 --> 00:27:06,747
Just throw it away.

358
00:27:11,085 --> 00:27:12,086
Seyun.

359
00:27:12,628 --> 00:27:13,629
What?

360
00:27:18,092 --> 00:27:19,134
Let's put an end to this.

361
00:27:20,010 --> 00:27:21,011
What?

362
00:27:25,891 --> 00:27:26,892
I want a divorce.

363
00:27:32,231 --> 00:27:33,857
I'm not getting divorced.

364
00:27:34,316 --> 00:27:35,401
What?

365
00:27:35,984 --> 00:27:37,486
I'm not getting divorced.

366
00:27:37,569 --> 00:27:40,739
You said no glue
can put it together, just like us.

367
00:27:41,365 --> 00:27:43,617
We're never going to be whole again.

368
00:27:44,660 --> 00:27:46,620
So why don't you want to get divorced?

369
00:27:51,333 --> 00:27:52,626
Because it's what you want.

370
00:27:54,169 --> 00:27:55,212
[scoffs]

371
00:27:56,088 --> 00:27:57,756
That's why you want to stay together?

372
00:27:58,424 --> 00:28:01,218
I don't want to give you
anything you want.

373
00:28:02,219 --> 00:28:04,596
I've made myself clear.
Let's get divorced.

374
00:28:07,808 --> 00:28:09,309
Well, try if you can.

375
00:28:10,352 --> 00:28:12,688
Guess you might get your wish
if one of us dies.

376
00:28:16,525 --> 00:28:17,735
[door closes]

377
00:28:43,135 --> 00:28:44,511
[sighs]

378
00:28:50,642 --> 00:28:51,685
CELEBRATING THE SUCCESS
STYLE
::cue()

379
00:28:51,769 --> 00:28:54,021
OF ARTIFICIAL SPINAL CORD TRANSPLANT
CLINICAL TRIAL

380
00:28:55,731 --> 00:28:57,983
What? Divorce? Are you serious?

381
00:28:59,985 --> 00:29:00,986
Yeah.

382
00:29:01,987 --> 00:29:04,198
You sure you gave this enough thought?

383
00:29:05,532 --> 00:29:08,660
Do you have any money saved up?
Are you going to start your own clinic?

384
00:29:09,745 --> 00:29:10,788
I don't know.

385
00:29:10,871 --> 00:29:12,122
How much do you have?

386
00:29:14,291 --> 00:29:15,918
Around 80 million won.

387
00:29:17,294 --> 00:29:19,213
You can't even get
an MRI scanner with that.

388
00:29:20,130 --> 00:29:22,424
Maybe a used X-ray machine at best.

389
00:29:23,133 --> 00:29:24,802
Then again, it's probably better

390
00:29:24,885 --> 00:29:27,471
than being half a director
under your father-in-law.

391
00:29:28,722 --> 00:29:30,390
Why don't you go find a salaried gig?

392
00:29:30,474 --> 00:29:32,643
You could rake in money off
physical therapy

393
00:29:32,726 --> 00:29:34,895
in a well-insured neighborhood.

394
00:29:35,771 --> 00:29:37,773
Or give people Botox
at a plastic surgery clinic.

395
00:29:40,734 --> 00:29:42,820
[no audible dialogue]

396
00:29:42,903 --> 00:29:44,988
I need to go talk to Dr. Ha over there.

397
00:29:45,072 --> 00:29:47,157
-We'll talk later.
-All right.

398
00:29:47,825 --> 00:29:48,909
-See you.
-Yeah.

399
00:30:02,881 --> 00:30:07,928
Uh… We finally showed
the world the fruit

400
00:30:08,512 --> 00:30:11,431
of all efforts we put in
throughout the past few years.

401
00:30:12,975 --> 00:30:19,273
And I'd like to thank each and every one
of you at Woori Together Medical Clinic.

402
00:30:19,356 --> 00:30:22,860
Let us celebrate this moment with a toast.

403
00:30:28,615 --> 00:30:29,616
Cheers!

404
00:30:29,700 --> 00:30:31,285
-Cheers!
-Cheers!

405
00:30:35,622 --> 00:30:37,165
[doctor] Congratulations, Dr. Kang.

406
00:30:37,249 --> 00:30:38,959
Incredible work, sir.

407
00:30:39,042 --> 00:30:40,168
Thanks.

408
00:30:41,295 --> 00:30:42,546
Hey, Taeju.

409
00:30:43,380 --> 00:30:44,423
Hey.

410
00:30:47,301 --> 00:30:48,802
Congratulations.

411
00:30:49,845 --> 00:30:50,846
Thanks.

412
00:30:53,181 --> 00:30:54,850
I know you worked really hard.

413
00:30:55,559 --> 00:30:58,020
-I'm glad it worked out.
-Yeah.

414
00:31:00,647 --> 00:31:01,940
-Talk to you later.
-Yeah.

415
00:31:09,531 --> 00:31:10,532
Congratulations.

416
00:31:12,534 --> 00:31:15,829
Your precious little project
became a huge success.

417
00:31:19,041 --> 00:31:20,083
This calls for a toast.

418
00:31:23,503 --> 00:31:24,504
What is it?

419
00:31:25,964 --> 00:31:27,633
You don't even want a toast with me?

420
00:31:32,596 --> 00:31:35,307
You don't want a toast
with a wife you want to divorce?

421
00:31:38,977 --> 00:31:40,437
What are you doing?

422
00:31:40,520 --> 00:31:41,897
This is not the place for this.

423
00:31:42,481 --> 00:31:44,191
Was it supposed to be a secret?

424
00:31:47,361 --> 00:31:48,403
I'm going to go, okay?

425
00:31:50,238 --> 00:31:51,490
Another emergency?

426
00:31:56,536 --> 00:31:57,537
Yeah.

427
00:31:58,497 --> 00:31:59,748
You should go, then.

428
00:32:01,124 --> 00:32:02,376
See you.

429
00:32:12,177 --> 00:32:14,596
[sighs]

430
00:32:14,680 --> 00:32:15,681
SEOKGI CHUEOTANG

431
00:32:15,764 --> 00:32:18,016
-All right, here's your credit card.
-[customer] Thank you.

432
00:32:18,100 --> 00:32:19,393
-See you again.
-Yeah.

433
00:32:19,476 --> 00:32:20,519
Taeyeong.

434
00:32:20,602 --> 00:32:23,605
Oh! What are you doing here?

435
00:32:23,689 --> 00:32:25,399
Mom, I'm here.

436
00:32:26,984 --> 00:32:28,443
Oh my, is that my baby?

437
00:32:28,527 --> 00:32:29,820
Hey, Taeju.

438
00:32:30,320 --> 00:32:32,447
Why didn't you give us a call?

439
00:32:32,531 --> 00:32:35,283
I was just passing by,
and I wanted to see you, Mom.

440
00:32:36,785 --> 00:32:39,287
Well, have you had dinner yet?

441
00:32:39,371 --> 00:32:40,539
No, not yet.

442
00:32:40,622 --> 00:32:42,499
Let me get a bowl of chueotang, Mom.

443
00:32:42,582 --> 00:32:44,584
-Wait right here, okay?
-Okay.

444
00:32:44,668 --> 00:32:47,379
You totally caught me off guard.

445
00:32:56,054 --> 00:32:57,848
Taeju, take these home.

446
00:33:00,642 --> 00:33:02,185
What's all this?

447
00:33:02,269 --> 00:33:05,230
Well, I made some spicy anchovies
and pickled cucumbers.

448
00:33:05,313 --> 00:33:07,983
And these are braised lotus roots
and black beans.

449
00:33:08,066 --> 00:33:09,860
They're all Seyun's favorites.

450
00:33:10,360 --> 00:33:12,029
Take them home and eat with her, okay?

451
00:33:12,487 --> 00:33:17,576
Oh, wow. When did you
prepare all this, Mom? [laughs]

452
00:33:18,577 --> 00:33:20,370
But Mom, this is too much food.

453
00:33:20,454 --> 00:33:23,623
I mean, we still have food
you gave us last time.

454
00:33:24,082 --> 00:33:27,836
Oh, no. It's not even that much.
I just used big containers.

455
00:33:27,919 --> 00:33:31,840
Seyun must be so busy these days.
She hasn't even been able to stop by.
STYLE
::cue()

456
00:33:31,923 --> 00:33:35,135
Make sure she eats
home-cooked meals when she's at home.

457
00:33:37,971 --> 00:33:42,017
But honestly, Seyun and I
rarely eat at home, so it's fine.

458
00:33:42,100 --> 00:33:43,685
If you don't want it, I'm taking it.

459
00:33:44,186 --> 00:33:45,562
What's wrong with you?

460
00:33:45,645 --> 00:33:48,857
-Don't take your little brother's stuff.
-[Taeyeong laughs]

461
00:33:50,442 --> 00:33:51,735
[mother] Just take it, all right?

462
00:33:53,779 --> 00:33:57,949
Make sure you take good care of Seyun.

463
00:34:01,495 --> 00:34:04,122
You need some home-cooked food
to keep you going.

464
00:34:05,082 --> 00:34:06,291
Okay?

465
00:34:17,385 --> 00:34:18,804
[sighs]

466
00:34:21,139 --> 00:34:22,140
Taeyeong.

467
00:34:23,350 --> 00:34:25,060
I'm really getting a divorce.

468
00:34:25,143 --> 00:34:26,770
Get it together.

469
00:34:27,729 --> 00:34:32,192
Mom may never say it out loud,
but you're basically her whole life.

470
00:34:32,275 --> 00:34:37,197
You used to throw a fit, saying
you could never live without your wife.

471
00:34:37,280 --> 00:34:40,242
And now you can't stand living with her?

472
00:34:41,326 --> 00:34:45,038
Look. Sometimes there are ups,
and sometimes there are downs.

473
00:34:45,956 --> 00:34:48,333
Marriage can be more volatile
than the stock market.

474
00:34:48,417 --> 00:34:50,127
That's just how it is.

475
00:34:50,669 --> 00:34:52,212
I know. I do.

476
00:34:52,295 --> 00:34:55,632
But it's not like I haven't tried
to make it work, and I don't…

477
00:34:57,342 --> 00:34:59,302
I don't know how it came to this.

478
00:35:00,137 --> 00:35:01,304
Trying isn't enough.

479
00:35:01,388 --> 00:35:05,308
You're sprinting to the left
when you should be going to the right.

480
00:35:05,851 --> 00:35:07,853
You'll just keep drifting away.

481
00:35:07,936 --> 00:35:09,062
Exactly.

482
00:35:10,522 --> 00:35:12,983
That's exactly what I'm trying to say.

483
00:35:13,066 --> 00:35:16,361
Honestly, I have no idea
what Seyun really wants.

484
00:35:20,615 --> 00:35:22,284
I'm done. I'm over it.

485
00:35:24,744 --> 00:35:27,414
I'm done trying just to be chewed out.

486
00:35:28,039 --> 00:35:29,624
I want to stop trying too.

487
00:35:31,001 --> 00:35:32,836
Let me tell you something about marriage.

488
00:35:33,837 --> 00:35:35,213
Even if you fight all the time,

489
00:35:35,297 --> 00:35:38,717
you must stick together
to find the right path.

490
00:35:56,776 --> 00:35:58,320
MONDAY, FEBRUARY 9

491
00:36:00,447 --> 00:36:03,074
[operator] Thank you for calling Olbareun,
the number one call service.

492
00:36:03,158 --> 00:36:04,826
Would you like to request a driver?

493
00:36:05,327 --> 00:36:09,706
Yeah, I'm at the Uil-dong Intersection.

494
00:36:14,294 --> 00:36:15,795
[knocking on window]

495
00:36:20,008 --> 00:36:22,010
[driver] Sir, did you call for a driver?

496
00:36:23,929 --> 00:36:26,848
Yeah, I did. Please take the wheel.

497
00:36:33,396 --> 00:36:34,940
[car door opens]

498
00:36:41,947 --> 00:36:43,365
[stammers]

499
00:36:44,574 --> 00:36:47,911
I feel like I made the call a second ago.
You got here so quickly.

500
00:36:47,994 --> 00:36:51,414
Well, I just happened to be in the area,
so I got here fast.

501
00:36:53,166 --> 00:36:54,417
Well, thank you.

502
00:36:54,501 --> 00:36:58,755
I guess today's just my lucky day.

503
00:37:40,088 --> 00:37:41,548
[front door opens]

504
00:37:59,983 --> 00:38:01,484
This isn't your room.

505
00:38:03,612 --> 00:38:04,613
Get out.

506
00:38:06,781 --> 00:38:08,658
This is my room, so get out.
STYLE
::cue()

507
00:38:15,248 --> 00:38:16,416
[alarm beeping]

508
00:38:23,214 --> 00:38:24,424
[groans]

509
00:38:26,468 --> 00:38:27,594
My head.

510
00:38:33,266 --> 00:38:34,434
[alarm stops]

511
00:38:39,356 --> 00:38:40,982
What's with all these notifications?

512
00:38:41,066 --> 00:38:42,609
MESSAGES
MISSED CALL

513
00:38:42,692 --> 00:38:45,737
HI, I'M YOUR DESIGNATED DRIVER
PLEASE REPLY WHEN YOU SEE THIS!

514
00:38:46,863 --> 00:38:48,073
[sighs]

515
00:38:48,948 --> 00:38:51,826
[sniffs] What the hell is this?

516
00:40:01,688 --> 00:40:03,231
[phone ringing]

517
00:40:03,898 --> 00:40:05,358
UNKNOWN NUMBER

518
00:40:08,528 --> 00:40:10,071
UNKNOWN NUMBER
DECLINE

519
00:40:13,575 --> 00:40:14,909
UNKNOWN NUMBER

520
00:40:20,582 --> 00:40:21,583
Yes, hello?

521
00:40:23,418 --> 00:40:24,419
Hello?

522
00:40:26,004 --> 00:40:27,297
Hello?

523
00:40:29,090 --> 00:40:31,092
-What the hell?
-Mr. Kang Taeju?

524
00:40:33,303 --> 00:40:34,804
Yes, speaking. Who's this?

525
00:40:35,430 --> 00:40:37,807
I'm the driver
who drove you to your house.

526
00:40:38,600 --> 00:40:39,642
Oh, yeah. Last night?

527
00:40:40,185 --> 00:40:41,895
Well, early this morning, sir.

528
00:40:41,978 --> 00:40:44,939
Oh, yes. So what's this about?

529
00:40:45,023 --> 00:40:48,568
I just wanted to ask
when you could pay me.

530
00:40:48,651 --> 00:40:51,571
Did I not pay you for the service?

531
00:40:52,781 --> 00:40:53,782
Sorry about that.

532
00:40:53,865 --> 00:40:56,534
If you could text me
your bank account number,

533
00:40:56,618 --> 00:40:59,078
I'll wire it to you right away.

534
00:40:59,162 --> 00:41:03,458
Actually, I'm not
talking about that money.

535
00:41:03,541 --> 00:41:04,542
I beg your pardon?

536
00:41:04,626 --> 00:41:07,086
-Your wife.
-My wife?

537
00:41:07,837 --> 00:41:09,756
Remember the job you asked me to do?

538
00:41:09,839 --> 00:41:11,841
I asked you to do something?

539
00:41:12,258 --> 00:41:13,343
Do you not remember?

540
00:41:13,968 --> 00:41:16,095
No, I don't remember
anything of that sort.

541
00:41:16,596 --> 00:41:19,349
Why is this prick playing dumb?

542
00:41:21,267 --> 00:41:22,602
What did you just call me?

543
00:41:23,436 --> 00:41:24,604
"Prick"?

544
00:41:24,687 --> 00:41:25,688
Listen.

545
00:41:25,772 --> 00:41:27,524
You better watch your mouth.

546
00:41:27,607 --> 00:41:29,859
-I said listen.
-You listen.

547
00:41:30,276 --> 00:41:32,529
If you don't apologize now,
I'm calling the cops.

548
00:41:32,612 --> 00:41:34,155
Mr. Kang Taeju!

549
00:41:34,739 --> 00:41:37,200
Don't be like this all of a sudden.

550
00:41:37,742 --> 00:41:39,410
You're making me real sad.

551
00:41:39,494 --> 00:41:44,207
I thought we were on the same page,
but if you keep playing dumb--

552
00:41:44,290 --> 00:41:47,335
-Okay, I'm hanging up.
-It's making me so sad.

553
00:41:47,418 --> 00:41:49,295
What is this nutjob…

554
00:41:50,755 --> 00:41:51,881
[sighs]

555
00:42:01,432 --> 00:42:03,268
Hey, Dr. Kang! Hey!

556
00:42:05,728 --> 00:42:07,230
What happened to your wife?

557
00:42:08,064 --> 00:42:09,107
What do you mean?

558
00:42:09,190 --> 00:42:10,775
She didn't show up to golf today.

559
00:42:12,569 --> 00:42:14,153
Seyun stood people up?

560
00:42:14,904 --> 00:42:17,323
God, do you know
what a tight spot she put me in?

561
00:42:18,324 --> 00:42:20,994
She begged me to set up the round
with the association president,

562
00:42:21,077 --> 00:42:22,787
and she flaked on me without a word.

563
00:42:23,162 --> 00:42:24,455
Just unbelievable…

564
00:42:25,665 --> 00:42:28,543
[driver] Your wife.
Remember the job you asked me to do?

565
00:42:28,626 --> 00:42:30,879
Why is this prick playing dumb?

566
00:42:31,504 --> 00:42:34,090
Chiung. Let's talk later, okay?

567
00:42:34,173 --> 00:42:35,258
[Dr. Choi] Okay.
STYLE
::cue()

568
00:42:39,345 --> 00:42:41,389
[phone ringing]

569
00:42:43,433 --> 00:42:46,436
Hey, what's going on?
Why did you stand up Chiung?

570
00:42:47,687 --> 00:42:48,980
[driver] Mr. Kang.

571
00:42:50,440 --> 00:42:53,318
How could you hang up on me like that?
I was talking.

572
00:42:54,485 --> 00:42:55,612
Who's this?

573
00:42:56,404 --> 00:42:58,865
It's me, the driver from earlier.

574
00:43:01,534 --> 00:43:02,535
I see.

575
00:43:03,494 --> 00:43:06,122
So why do you have my wife's phone?

576
00:43:08,499 --> 00:43:10,293
I can't believe you.

577
00:43:12,879 --> 00:43:15,006
What… What the hell do you want?

578
00:43:16,341 --> 00:43:18,676
Where's my wife? Put her on the phone.

579
00:43:18,760 --> 00:43:20,178
You're making me so sad…

580
00:43:21,346 --> 00:43:22,639
I think I'm going to tear up.

581
00:43:23,139 --> 00:43:25,016
Put my wife on the phone right now!

582
00:43:25,099 --> 00:43:26,392
[call disconnects]

583
00:43:27,060 --> 00:43:28,478
[phone buzzes]

584
00:43:30,438 --> 00:43:32,565
UNKNOWN NUMBER

585
00:43:35,777 --> 00:43:36,778
[phone buzzes]

586
00:43:36,861 --> 00:43:38,738
Anyway, that being said…

587
00:43:42,200 --> 00:43:44,285
I want you to get rid of my wife.

588
00:43:44,369 --> 00:43:45,370
[driver] What did you say?

589
00:43:45,453 --> 00:43:47,038
[Taeju] I'll pay you, okay?

590
00:43:47,121 --> 00:43:49,040
I'll pay you 300… No.

591
00:43:49,123 --> 00:43:52,043
I'll pay you 500 million won, so please.

592
00:43:52,126 --> 00:43:56,381
[driver]
So you want me to get rid of your wife?

593
00:43:56,464 --> 00:43:57,465
Yeah.

594
00:44:01,761 --> 00:44:04,514
UNKNOWN NUMBER

595
00:44:04,597 --> 00:44:06,599
[phone buzzing]

596
00:44:09,644 --> 00:44:11,688
[driver]
Did you see the picture and the video?

597
00:44:12,313 --> 00:44:14,440
Yes, I did.

598
00:44:17,443 --> 00:44:19,779
But my wife…

599
00:44:20,488 --> 00:44:21,489
You didn't…

600
00:44:23,449 --> 00:44:25,201
It's not what I think, right?

601
00:44:25,785 --> 00:44:27,370
Unfortunately…

602
00:44:27,453 --> 00:44:28,746
Your wife is

603
00:44:29,872 --> 00:44:31,165
still alive.

604
00:44:32,166 --> 00:44:33,167
[sighs]

605
00:44:33,251 --> 00:44:37,964
But I'll take care of her
as soon as you send me the money,

606
00:44:38,047 --> 00:44:39,173
so don't worry about it.

607
00:44:39,257 --> 00:44:41,759
Hold on a minute, sir. It's just…

608
00:44:42,802 --> 00:44:45,346
Why are you doing this to us?

609
00:44:45,430 --> 00:44:47,849
I could ask you the same thing!

610
00:44:47,932 --> 00:44:49,350
Why are you doing this?

611
00:44:49,434 --> 00:44:52,228
You can't put me up to something
and pretend you don't remember!

612
00:44:53,688 --> 00:44:55,565
Look, I never put you up to…

613
00:44:58,067 --> 00:45:00,945
I don't know
what you're talking about, okay?

614
00:45:01,029 --> 00:45:03,322
You're only making things
more difficult, boss.

615
00:45:03,406 --> 00:45:06,075
And this video. Is that even me?

616
00:45:06,159 --> 00:45:07,910
This has to be fake.

617
00:45:07,994 --> 00:45:09,328
Is that what you think?

618
00:45:17,378 --> 00:45:18,629
No, I mean…

619
00:45:18,713 --> 00:45:21,090
Listen, I may have said
some things I didn't mean

620
00:45:21,674 --> 00:45:23,634
because I was drunk,

621
00:45:23,718 --> 00:45:27,180
but you shouldn't have taken it seriously.

622
00:45:27,263 --> 00:45:28,264
And?

623
00:45:29,307 --> 00:45:31,851
Please let my wife go. I'm begging you.

624
00:45:31,934 --> 00:45:32,935
Sir.

625
00:45:33,019 --> 00:45:36,731
First, you want me to kill her,
and now you want me to let her live?

626
00:45:36,814 --> 00:45:38,316
Yes, please don't kill her.

627
00:45:38,399 --> 00:45:42,570
If you just let her go,
I won't tell a soul about what happened.

628
00:45:42,653 --> 00:45:44,572
Here's the thing, boss.

629
00:45:44,655 --> 00:45:48,201
I hate it when people
make things complicated.

630
00:45:48,618 --> 00:45:52,371
People who don't keep their promises?
I just can't stand them.

631
00:45:52,455 --> 00:45:56,459
I'm going to ask you one last time,
so really think before you answer.

632
00:45:58,086 --> 00:46:01,672
Do you want your wife dead or alive?

633
00:46:01,756 --> 00:46:05,343
I want her to live. Let her live. Please.

634
00:46:05,426 --> 00:46:06,427
All right, then.

635
00:46:06,511 --> 00:46:09,514
-I'll let it slide this time…
-[sighs]

636
00:46:09,597 --> 00:46:11,307
…but don't let this happen again.

637
00:46:11,390 --> 00:46:15,853
Yes, of course.
Thank you so much. Thank you.

638
00:46:15,937 --> 00:46:18,856
But you know
there'll be extra charges, right?

639
00:46:18,940 --> 00:46:20,733
You changed the options.

640
00:46:21,609 --> 00:46:22,693
What options?

641
00:46:22,777 --> 00:46:27,031
It's 500 million to kill your wife,
and 1 billion won to let her live.

642
00:46:27,740 --> 00:46:29,325
You have three hours.

643
00:46:29,408 --> 00:46:30,409
What?

644
00:46:30,493 --> 00:46:34,580
If I don't get my one billion won
in three hours, consider your wife dead.

645
00:46:34,664 --> 00:46:38,793
And if you go to the cops
or ignore my calls, she's dead.

646
00:46:38,876 --> 00:46:40,211
Hold on, three hours is too--

647
00:46:40,294 --> 00:46:42,630
Now, you won't be able
to reach your wife's phone.

648
00:46:42,713 --> 00:46:47,510
It's 10:25 a.m. right now,
and I'll be in touch in three hours.

649
00:46:47,593 --> 00:46:48,803
And, boss?

650
00:46:49,387 --> 00:46:51,097
Don't disappoint me anymore.

651
00:46:51,180 --> 00:46:52,431
Hello?

652
00:46:52,515 --> 00:46:54,142
Hello?

653
00:46:54,225 --> 00:46:55,268
Hello?
STYLE
::cue()

654
00:47:02,400 --> 00:47:03,568
WOORI TOGETHER MEDICAL CENTER

655
00:47:03,651 --> 00:47:05,695
[Taeju] I want you to get rid of my wife.

656
00:47:06,737 --> 00:47:08,322
I'll pay you, okay?

657
00:47:08,739 --> 00:47:11,325
I'll pay you 300… No.

658
00:47:11,409 --> 00:47:13,327
I'll pay you 500 million won, so please.

659
00:47:15,079 --> 00:47:19,584
So you want me to get rid of your wife?

660
00:47:22,086 --> 00:47:23,129
Yeah.

661
00:47:25,798 --> 00:47:28,426
[operator] Thank you for calling Olbareun,
the number one call service.

662
00:47:28,509 --> 00:47:32,138
[Taeju]
Yeah, I'm at the Uil-dong Intersection.

663
00:47:32,221 --> 00:47:33,931
[knocking on window]

664
00:47:34,682 --> 00:47:38,227
Yeah, I did. Please take the wheel.

665
00:47:42,190 --> 00:47:44,567
I definitely saw his face.

666
00:47:46,194 --> 00:47:48,362
But I don't remember it.

667
00:47:59,207 --> 00:48:00,458
[car beeps]

668
00:48:21,437 --> 00:48:22,521
CALLING

669
00:48:22,605 --> 00:48:24,815
[phone ringing]

670
00:48:29,070 --> 00:48:31,239
-[person] Hello?
-Hello?

671
00:48:31,322 --> 00:48:37,036
Is this the driver
who drove me home last night?

672
00:48:37,119 --> 00:48:38,246
Oh, Uil-dong Intersection?

673
00:48:38,329 --> 00:48:40,081
Why didn't you answer your phone?

674
00:48:40,164 --> 00:48:41,582
Nobody was there when I got there.

675
00:48:41,666 --> 00:48:43,042
[disconnects call]

676
00:48:48,881 --> 00:48:51,509
[operator] Thank you for calling Olbareun,
the number one call service.

677
00:48:51,592 --> 00:48:53,135
Would you like to request a driver?

678
00:48:53,219 --> 00:48:57,390
Hi. I'm looking for the driver
who drove me home last night.

679
00:48:57,473 --> 00:49:00,226
And you called from this number, correct?

680
00:49:00,309 --> 00:49:02,395
-Yeah.
-Just a moment.

681
00:49:03,521 --> 00:49:06,941
It seems like this request was canceled
because the driver couldn't reach you.

682
00:49:07,024 --> 00:49:10,027
No. I definitely used
your service last night.

683
00:49:10,111 --> 00:49:11,988
According to our records,

684
00:49:12,071 --> 00:49:15,157
your designated driver called you
three times at 1:47 a.m. this morning

685
00:49:15,241 --> 00:49:19,287
but gave up and accepted another customer.

686
00:49:19,370 --> 00:49:21,789
What? I didn't pick up?

687
00:49:22,248 --> 00:49:24,333
It looks like you called
for another driver too.

688
00:49:24,417 --> 00:49:26,252
Please contact the other service provider.

689
00:49:26,335 --> 00:49:27,962
I… Wait.

690
00:50:21,932 --> 00:50:24,310
SEONGJIN POLICE STATION

691
00:50:32,401 --> 00:50:34,195
[phone buzzing]

692
00:50:38,491 --> 00:50:40,159
INCOMING VIDEO CALL
UNKNOWN NUMBER

693
00:50:40,242 --> 00:50:41,911
[Seyun screams]
STYLE
::cue()

694
00:50:43,871 --> 00:50:45,414
[stammering] Seyun.

695
00:50:46,374 --> 00:50:51,420
What are you… What the hell are you doing?

696
00:50:51,504 --> 00:50:52,630
Honey.

697
00:50:53,589 --> 00:50:55,716
No! Stop it! No!

698
00:50:56,342 --> 00:50:58,052
Sir, what are you doing?

699
00:50:58,135 --> 00:51:00,638
Please! Please don't do that!

700
00:51:00,721 --> 00:51:02,973
Please pull her up! Please, sir!

701
00:51:03,057 --> 00:51:05,017
[Seyun screaming]

702
00:51:05,101 --> 00:51:06,102
Seyun…

703
00:51:08,896 --> 00:51:10,231
Are you out of your mind?

704
00:51:10,314 --> 00:51:11,732
What the hell are you doing?

705
00:51:13,192 --> 00:51:16,946
[driver] You're the one who broke the deal
and tried to go to the cops.

706
00:51:17,029 --> 00:51:18,447
Did you think I wouldn't know?

707
00:51:23,744 --> 00:51:25,830
Why do you keep
disappointing me like this?

708
00:51:31,627 --> 00:51:33,254
I'm sorry, sir.

709
00:51:34,380 --> 00:51:36,882
You should be thanking me right now.

710
00:51:38,008 --> 00:51:42,972
Your wife could have died,
and I stopped that.

711
00:51:43,055 --> 00:51:44,223
Right.

712
00:51:44,306 --> 00:51:48,102
There's only so much
a person can tolerate.

713
00:51:48,727 --> 00:51:51,188
And I've reached my limit.

714
00:51:55,025 --> 00:51:56,152
I'm very sorry, sir.

715
00:51:57,778 --> 00:52:00,739
It looks like I gave you too much time.

716
00:52:00,823 --> 00:52:04,743
Let me fix that so you don't get
any more stupid ideas.

717
00:52:04,827 --> 00:52:05,828
What?

718
00:52:05,911 --> 00:52:08,914
You have one hour to get my one billion.

719
00:52:09,415 --> 00:52:12,293
Sir, one hour is far too short.

720
00:52:12,835 --> 00:52:14,211
I said what I said.

721
00:52:14,753 --> 00:52:15,754
CALL ENDED

722
00:52:15,838 --> 00:52:17,715
Hello? Hello…

723
00:52:48,078 --> 00:52:49,413
CALLING
FATHER-IN-LAW

724
00:52:49,497 --> 00:52:51,957
The number you dialed is not available…

725
00:52:52,041 --> 00:52:53,209
HOSPITAL FRONT DESK

726
00:52:54,543 --> 00:52:56,545
Woori Together Medical Center.
How may I help you?

727
00:52:56,629 --> 00:52:58,047
Hi, it's Kang Taeju here.

728
00:52:58,464 --> 00:53:00,466
Is Dr. Ko at the hospital right now?

729
00:53:00,549 --> 00:53:04,553
Dr. Ko is currently in surgery.

730
00:53:08,432 --> 00:53:10,017
[dialing]

731
00:53:10,100 --> 00:53:11,810
The number you dialed is not available…

732
00:53:11,894 --> 00:53:12,895
CALLING
MOTHER-IN-LAW

733
00:53:20,402 --> 00:53:22,947
MODU BANK

734
00:53:30,079 --> 00:53:32,456
-Dr. Kang, long time no see.
-Hi.

735
00:53:33,332 --> 00:53:34,792
So, how have you been?

736
00:53:35,668 --> 00:53:39,421
Actually, I need
to take out a loan urgently.

737
00:53:39,505 --> 00:53:40,506
Okay.

738
00:53:40,923 --> 00:53:43,175
How much are you looking to take out?

739
00:53:43,551 --> 00:53:46,095
Well, I'd like to withdraw
all 80 million from my account,

740
00:53:46,178 --> 00:53:48,389
and I need an additional 920 million.

741
00:53:49,139 --> 00:53:50,349
Did you say 920 million won?

742
00:53:50,432 --> 00:53:52,017
Yeah, and…

743
00:53:53,227 --> 00:53:55,354
Could I get it within 50 minutes?

744
00:53:55,437 --> 00:53:59,108
I'm sorry, but even for our VIP clients,

745
00:53:59,191 --> 00:54:02,736
it'll take at least two weeks
for the papers to be approved.

746
00:54:02,820 --> 00:54:07,700
You probably couldn't even take out
a private loan that big on the same day.
STYLE
::cue()

747
00:54:25,718 --> 00:54:27,594
RECENT CALLS

748
00:54:43,152 --> 00:54:46,322
STOP BEFORE CROSSING

749
00:54:46,405 --> 00:54:47,531
STOP

750
00:54:47,614 --> 00:54:48,699
TRAIN APPROACHING

751
00:54:48,782 --> 00:54:50,326
TRAIN PASSING
STOP

752
00:55:20,481 --> 00:55:23,192
[phone buzzing]

753
00:55:23,275 --> 00:55:25,986
INCOMING VIDEO CALL
UNKNOWN NUMBER

754
00:55:34,620 --> 00:55:35,704
Hello?

755
00:55:36,413 --> 00:55:37,456
[driver] Hey, boss.

756
00:55:37,539 --> 00:55:39,208
It's almost time.

757
00:55:43,379 --> 00:55:44,922
Is my wife okay?

758
00:55:45,005 --> 00:55:46,840
She's fine for now.

759
00:55:46,924 --> 00:55:48,509
And my one billion won?

760
00:55:50,010 --> 00:55:52,554
Yeah. I have it.

761
00:55:52,638 --> 00:55:54,556
Let me see it.

762
00:55:58,018 --> 00:55:59,520
Each contains 500 million.

763
00:56:00,938 --> 00:56:02,272
One billion in total.

764
00:56:02,356 --> 00:56:05,067
I wouldn't expect any less
from a director at a hospital.

765
00:56:05,150 --> 00:56:10,030
I mean, honestly, most people could
never even see a billion won in cash.

766
00:56:10,114 --> 00:56:11,615
Where do I take it?

767
00:56:11,698 --> 00:56:13,784
I forgot to tell you that.

768
00:56:14,535 --> 00:56:17,830
Come to 43-87, Sajiro-gil.

769
00:56:18,247 --> 00:56:21,667
Be here within 30 minutes,
and you have to come alone.

770
00:56:22,084 --> 00:56:24,586
You know that's the only way
to save your wife, right?

771
00:56:25,087 --> 00:56:26,380
I'll be waiting.

772
00:56:33,512 --> 00:56:35,597
[automated voice] Up ahead, turn right.

773
00:56:39,184 --> 00:56:41,645
Entering school zone.
Please drive carefully.

774
00:56:41,728 --> 00:56:44,273
SCHOOL ZONE

775
00:56:47,734 --> 00:56:49,778
In 400 meters, keep straight.

776
00:56:57,035 --> 00:56:59,079
Turn left.

777
00:57:06,795 --> 00:57:09,173
In 300 meters, keep straight.
STYLE
::cue()

778
00:57:13,844 --> 00:57:15,387
Up ahead, turn right.

779
00:57:20,142 --> 00:57:23,562
Take the slight left into the alley.
Then, turn left.

780
00:57:25,939 --> 00:57:28,358
Continue straight to 43, Sajiro-gil.

781
00:57:29,151 --> 00:57:31,069
Please drive safely.

782
00:57:34,865 --> 00:57:36,658
Up ahead, turn left.

783
00:57:39,620 --> 00:57:41,705
[horn honking]

784
00:57:46,376 --> 00:57:48,837
[panting]

785
00:58:01,016 --> 00:58:02,768
Hey, are you okay?

786
00:58:04,269 --> 00:58:07,105
Hey! Can you hear me?

787
00:58:11,360 --> 00:58:12,528
Let me call an ambulance.

788
00:58:13,237 --> 00:58:14,363
Just hang in there.

789
00:58:16,281 --> 00:58:17,574
Hey, my…

790
00:58:18,075 --> 00:58:20,369
-Yes?
-[panting]

791
00:58:21,203 --> 00:58:22,996
My one billion won…

792
00:58:24,665 --> 00:58:25,666
What was that?

793
00:58:26,041 --> 00:58:28,168
[slurring] Did you bring my billion won?

794
00:58:28,794 --> 00:58:31,838
What? I can't hear you.
Can you speak up a little?

795
00:58:33,298 --> 00:58:35,008
[clearly]
I said, did you bring my billion won?

796
00:58:44,184 --> 00:58:49,106
THE HUSBAND

797
00:59:29,229 --> 00:59:30,814
[detective]
You know where Ms. Ko is, don't you?

798
00:59:30,897 --> 00:59:32,482
[driver] I'm going to your wife now.

799
00:59:32,566 --> 00:59:35,027
There's no time to be screwing around!

800
00:59:35,694 --> 00:59:37,362
This guy is a psycho!

801
00:59:37,446 --> 00:59:38,905
My wife's in danger!

802
00:59:38,989 --> 00:59:41,658
Let me out of here! [screams]

803
00:59:41,742 --> 00:59:43,452
Who are you? What do you want?

804
00:59:43,535 --> 00:59:46,079
[driver] If you disappoint me
with another dumb stunt,

805
00:59:46,163 --> 00:59:48,624
you will pay for it dearly.

806
00:59:48,707 --> 00:59:51,251
I can actually get you the money you want.
I promise. I swear.

807
00:59:51,335 --> 00:59:53,670
[person] You can have this
on top of the original two billion.

808
00:59:53,754 --> 00:59:55,297
-[driver] Just because you're rich…
-Honey!

809
00:59:55,380 --> 00:59:56,673
You think you can mock me?

810
00:59:58,634 --> 01:00:01,136
What happened to your wife is all on you.

811
01:00:01,219 --> 01:00:03,221
Translated by Hyun Sik Yoon

